Z||000000||Old Lar||05-03-2000||09:44 PM||||American Heart Association is having a function at Watkins Glenn 5/13/00.  There is an opportunity to drive the track.  It may be a parade lap or two, I haven't got the details.<P>1-800-242-6965  talk to a machine, but you want to speak to Lee Lamoreau for details.<P>I understand it $10 for entry, track time noon to 5pm.||||reg||7
Z||000001||theogre||05-04-2000||06:28 PM||||God, The glen,,,,,,, I haven't been to that area in years. Does Corning still own it? They did a nice job cleaning it up after it was closed. Wish I could make that trip.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||05-05-2000||12:52 AM||||I love watching the Winston Cup cars run the Bud at the Glenn. I just had to get out my pedals and steering wheel and took a few laps on Nascar 3. I could not imagine how much fun it would be taking my Fiero around that place.||||reg||1
Z||000003||RossT||05-05-2000||02:46 AM||||I have a numbered print of "fiero at watkins glenn" Came with the gt I bought last year.  Never new where it was!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||05-05-2000||02:39 PM||||Ross, It's in the Finger Lakes reagon upstate. Years ago it used to be the only U.S. F1 stop. Then the track got really bad, F1 left and the track closed. By this time neither decent fans nor drivers wanted anything to do with the place. It was a horrible mess and had been drawing really ugly crowds for some time. (They used to steal cars from the parking lot, push them in the mud hole, and set fire to them.)<P>Corning Glass, in Corning N.Y., bought the track and spent a fortune on it. If Corning hadn't bought it it was likely going to be lost to history along with our cars. (The mud hole was filled in, and the ugly crowds are not permitted. Corning took this project very seriously.) I don't know if Corning still owns it or not but the track thankfully has become very popular with both race fans and drivers once again. There is no other permanant road coarse of this class in the country that I know of.<P>I wish I would have had more notice so I could go to this. Anyone that can go should. Even a slow lap at this track is likely a once in a lifetime event.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Old Lar||05-05-2000||04:45 PM||||Lee just got back to me.  He talked to my machine.  The $10 is for three controlled laps at the track.  I spoke to someone who did this last year in their Fiero and they had a hard time keeping up with the pace car.  It is a road course and has some 180 + degree turns.  Watkins Glenn is on rt 414 north of Corning, NY. It is at the south end of Seneca Lake in NY's wine country.  A portion of the $10 goes to the heart fund, and there is a walk in the morning for the heart fund.<P>This is a rare opportunity to drive on an international race track and see a scenic part of upstate NY.||||reg||6
Z||000006||Fformula88||05-09-2000||03:17 PM||||Old Lar...  Do you know if there are other events at the track?  Also, is there a general admission to the track, and a $10 to drive, or is it an all for $10 deal?  Just wondering since you got the message.  If not I'll go ahead and call them.||||reg||5
Z||000007||Old Lar||05-09-2000||07:35 PM||||The only thing the message said was that this was the opening of the track for the year.  There was  to be a walk for the heart association and that he'd like me to join the walk.  I'm not much into walking for causes, but I donate the $10 just to drive on the track even at controlled speeds.  I've done Daytona, Gateway International, and Raceway Park.  I'd like to add Watkins Glenn, just to say I did it.<P>I called my local POCI club (Pontiac Oakland Club International) and she said the whole club did the cruise when the track reopened in 1986 and it was fun.<P>Nothing else was scheduled at the track that I know of, maybe some sort of flea market.<P>I'm going to try to get some photos of my car at the track, cruise around, check out the town and see whats happening!||||reg||10
Z||000008||Old Lar||05-13-2000||08:45 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/WatkinsglenM.jpg"> <P>Me on the track.  The rain stopped, the sky cleared and I got to drive on the track.  I used second and third gear mostly.  Not much over 60mpg.  It was controlled laps.  I wished I could have spent more time.||||reg||6
